- How would you test the rollback plan without impacting production?
- What metrics and alerts would validate containment efficacy during an incident?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical CMK usage, Key Vault integration, identity access, policy enforcement, and rollback planning at beginner level.

## Key Concepts
- Customer-managed keys (CMK) for storage at rest
- Azure Key Vault with managed identities
- Storage Account encryption properties and keyVaultProperties
- Azure Policy to require CMK on new storage accounts
- Canary rollout and rollback strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// ARM-like snippet illustrating CMK encryption on a storage account
{
  "type": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts",
  "name": "[storageAccountName]",
  "apiVersion": "2023-01-01",
  "location": "[resourceGroup().location]",
  "properties": {
    "encryption": {
      "keySource": "Microsoft.KeyVault",
      "keyVaultProperties": {
        "keyName": "<cmk-name>",
        "keyVaultUri": "https://<vault-name>.vault.azure.net/"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate CMK policy compliance in CI/CD? 
- How would you handle CMK rotation without downtime?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design automated IR in Azure at scale, integrating Key Vault, Sentinel, Runbooks, and network isolation.

## Key Concepts

- Key Vault rotation and secret versioning
- Azure Sentinel detection rules and alerting
- Automation Runbooks or Logic Apps
- Private Endpoints and NSGs
- Azure AD session revocation and PIM

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-IR runbook snippet (Azure SDK)
async function rotateSecret(vaultName, secretName){
  const newValue = generateSecret();
  await secretClient.setSecret(vaultName, secretName, newValue);
  await aadClient.revokeUserSessions('compromised-id');
}
```

